{
 "_comment": "The two tank hierarchies of ADR 4.3, read from two books and compared. 4.3.3.1.2 is a hierarchy of codes and applies to gases; 4.3.4.1.2 is the rationalized approach and applies to classes 3 to 9, where a tank code names the group of substances it may carry by class, classification code and packing group, and inherits the groups of the codes below it. A cell the two readings do not agree on carries both values under 'disputed' and settles nothing.",
